{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-128085",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk: go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/log: go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace: OpenTelemetry-Go: Denial of Service via attribute truncation bypass using Unicode replacement characters"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OpenTelemetry-Go is the Go implementation of OpenTelemetry. From SDK version 1.33.0, SDK log version 0.9.0, and trace version 1.35.0 until version 1.47.0, the AttributeValueLengthLimit and WithAttributeValueLengthLimit truncation paths in sdk/internal/attrnorm, sdk/log/internal/attrnorm, and trace/auto.go do not count valid U+FFFD replacement characters. This is a distinct incomplete-fix defect in the replacement truncation code introduced by the remediation for CVE-2026-81869. Values composed of or dominated by those characters can therefore exceed the configured character and memory bound in span, log-record, and auto-instrumentation trace attributes. Attacker-controlled telemetry attributes can increase retained memory and pipeline pressure, while confidentiality and integrity are not affected. This issue is fixed in version 1.47.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-128085",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-128085\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace\nFixed Version: 1.47.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-128085](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-128085)\nOpenTelemetry-Go is the Go implementation of OpenTelemetry. From SDK version 1.33.0, SDK log version 0.9.0, and trace version 1.35.0 until version 1.47.0, the AttributeValueLengthLimit and WithAttributeValueLengthLimit truncation paths in sdk/internal/attrnorm, sdk/log/internal/attrnorm, and trace/auto.go do not count valid U+FFFD replacement characters. This is a distinct incomplete-fix defect in the replacement truncation code introduced by the remediation for CVE-2026-81869. Values composed of or dominated by those characters can therefore exceed the configured character and memory bound in span, log-record, and auto-instrumentation trace attributes. Attacker-controlled telemetry attributes can increase retained memory and pipeline pressure, while confidentiality and integrity are not affected. This issue is fixed in version 1.47.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-128085**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace|1.47.0|[CVE-2026-128085](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-128085)|\n\nOpenTelemetry-Go is the Go implementation of OpenTelemetry. From SDK version 1.33.0, SDK log version 0.9.0, and trace version 1.35.0 until version 1.47.0, the AttributeValueLengthLimit and WithAttributeValueLengthLimit truncation paths in sdk/internal/attrnorm, sdk/log/internal/attrnorm, and trace/auto.go do not count valid U+FFFD replacement characters. This is a distinct incomplete-fix defect in the replacement truncation code introduced by the remediation for CVE-2026-81869. Values composed of or dominated by those characters can therefore exceed the configured character and memory bound in span, log-record, and auto-instrumentation trace attributes. Attacker-controlled telemetry attributes can increase retained memory and pipeline pressure, while confidentiality and integrity are not affected. This issue is fixed in version 1.47.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.3,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56864",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "golang.org/x/mod/sumdb: golang.org/x/mod/sumdb: Integrity bypass via malicious GOSUMDB"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A malicious GOSUMDB was capable of serving arbitrary module content not contained within the transparency log. This attack allows for a coordinating GOPROXY and GOSUMDB to serve a client malicious module content that cannot be detected by evaluating the transparency log. In order to determine if you have been affected:   rm -r go.sum go.work.sum vendor/ && go mod tidy"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-56864",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-56864\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: golang.org/x/mod\nFixed Version: 0.40.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-56864](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-56864)\nA malicious GOSUMDB was capable of serving arbitrary module content not contained within the transparency log. This attack allows for a coordinating GOPROXY and GOSUMDB to serve a client malicious module content that cannot be detected by evaluating the transparency log. In order to determine if you have been affected:   rm -r go.sum go.work.sum vendor/ && go mod tidy",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-56864**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|golang.org/x/mod|0.40.0|[CVE-2026-56864](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-56864)|\n\nA malicious GOSUMDB was capable of serving arbitrary module content not contained within the transparency log. This attack allows for a coordinating GOPROXY and GOSUMDB to serve a client malicious module content that cannot be detected by evaluating the transparency log. In order to determine if you have been affected:   rm -r go.sum go.work.sum vendor/ && go mod tidy"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.76.1"
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CVE-2026-128085",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
